  {
    "episode_id": 92704,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92704.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm in house leadership now, so as a member of house leadership, but I was asked to do that, so I did. And I think the kids were a little more interested in Barack Obama, so we talked a little bit more about that. The story I think they liked the best is I asked them if they knew what Air Force One was, and most of the kids knew that these are the older kids. You know, the preschoolers, we didn't get into this deep of a conversation. And so I said I flew with President Obama on Air Force One and then I asked if they knew what Marine One was and most of them did and I said well that's this helicopter and I said I also flew on Marine One with President Obama. So we just told little stories and my closing message was You know, because they liked President Obama, I said President Obama grew up with a single mom and through learning and reading. He accomplished and went all the way to the presidency. So that was my message. If you learn, if you read, you can do anything you want. And then we went over the...",
